### Skills (`.claude/skills/`)

Reusable workflows invoked via `/command`:

| Skill | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `/start-session` | Read SESSION_LOG + NEXT_STEPS + git state. Print 5-line briefing. |
| `/self-review` | Comprehensive pre-PR review: sanity gates + deep file review. |
| `/commit` | Conventional commit with secrets scanning and format validation. |
| `/new-feature <name>` | Scaffold a feature module across all relevant stacks. |
| `/local-setup [mode]` | Bootstrap, doctor, or reset the dev environment. |
| `/deploy [env]` | Trigger release workflow via GitHub Actions. |
| `/adr <title>` | Create an Architecture Decision Record in `docs/adr/`. |
| `/sync-docs` | Sync SESSION_LOG + NEXT_STEPS + CLAUDE.md after decisions. |
| `/plan-review` | Challenge a plan with engineering rigor before coding. |

### Hooks (`.claude/hooks/`)

Automated behaviors that run on every session:

| Hook | Trigger | Purpose |
|------|---------|---------|
| `format-on-edit.cjs` | PostToolUse (Edit/Write) | Auto-format files after Claude edits them |
| `block-dangerous-bash.cjs` | PreToolUse (Bash) | Block `rm -rf`, force push, `--no-verify`, global installs |
| `session-context.cjs` | SessionStart | Inject git state, ticket ID, and welcome message |

### Settings (`.claude/settings.json`)

Project-level Claude Code settings:
- Hooks wired to the 3 hook scripts above
- Permission allowlist for safe Bash commands (stack-specific)

### Supporting files

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `welcome-message.md` | Greeting shown at session start with skill quick reference |
| `hints.txt` | Pool of tips shown randomly at session start |

## For humans

These tools work for human developers too. Type `/` in Claude Code to see available skills. The rules and conventions in `CLAUDE.md` and the path-scoped rules apply to all code in the project, whether written by humans or AI.

### Recommended workflow

1. Start a session: `/start-session`
2. Plan your work: describe the feature, use the `architect` agent for complex changes
3. Implement: use `/new-feature` to scaffold, write code following the rules
4. Review: `/self-review` before pushing
5. Commit: `/commit` for clean conventional commits
6. Document: `/sync-docs` to keep project docs current
